# 13. Final Engineering Assessment

The current branch makes meaningful progress toward reducing unnecessary Firestore reads, especially in the examination autosave path and in dashboards that previously fetched broad collections.

The main engineering decision was to reduce redundant reads at their source rather than rely on mirroring or a browser-only database switch. That approach is necessary because read reduction benefits every user, while mirroring alone does not guarantee that requests move away from an exhausted database.

However, the current implementation remains an initial optimisation pass. Several query paths still require schema validation, broad areas of the repository have not yet been audited, Monitoring has not been verified against the actual quota meter, and coordinated database failover remains unfinished.

The latest general Quality Gate passed, but the Assessment Quality Gate and Firestore Rules Tests are blocked by the inconsistent lockfile, and the Netlify preview failed. These issues must be resolved before release.

**Current release decision: do not merge or deploy this revision yet.**

